From c332213927c984ca6a4fd0fc843c630f201ccca3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 22:54:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] trans: on macOS, look for lib<name>.dylib before lib<name>.a
 at the final link

The explicit library lookup at the executable link (fcfbf16e) checks
lib<name>.so, then lib<name>.a, in each crate's link directories. On
Darwin no library is a .so, so any directory that has both the dylib and
the archive links the archive. Apple's ld takes the dylib first.

openssl-sys finds MacPorts openssl3 (OPENSSL_DIR=${prefix}/libexec/openssl3,
or ${prefix} via the openssl port), sees libssl.a and libssl.dylib, and
asks for `rustc-link-lib=dylib=ssl`. minicargo drops the kind and mrustc
linked ${prefix}/libexec/openssl3/lib/libssl.a and libcrypto.a into the
executable. MacPorts builds libcrypto with zlib, and nothing on the link
line asks for -lz. The same goes for libz-sys (pkg-config gives
-L${prefix}/lib, MacPorts zlib installs libz.a) and libsqlite3-sys.

Check lib<name>.dylib first on macOS targets. Vendored builds (cc::Build,
openssl-src) only produce archives, so they still link statically.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/trans/codegen_c.cpp | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/trans/codegen_c.cpp b/src/trans/codegen_c.cpp
index f0f236f6..63ca8bfd 100644
--- a/src/trans/codegen_c.cpp
+++ b/src/trans/codegen_c.cpp
@@ -1213,6 +1213,13 @@ namespace {
                     {
                         std::string lib_path;
                         if( !is_windows ) {
+                            // Apple's ld takes the dylib before the archive in each directory. Installed libraries
+                            // often have both (e.g. MacPorts openssl3), so don't link them statically by accident.
+                            if( Target_GetCurSpec().m_os_name == "macos" ) {
+                                lib_path = FMT(path << "/lib" << name << ".dylib");
+                                if( file_exists(lib_path) )
+                                    return lib_path;
+                            }
                             lib_path = FMT(path << "/lib" << name << ".so");
                             if( file_exists(lib_path) )
                                 return lib_path;
